[{:db/id "q-348756/field-1/074131e71753d30c82ed90c556f57c3329d4ace9bd4331e7a888efe975b52fc4" :answer/id #uuid "61404ce4-ecb2-5ab7-bff5-3dc72be79709" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15\\pi}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348756/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ac414bdb-1e9c-501d-94fc-5ad66fcd3a37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348756/field-1/074131e71753d30c82ed90c556f57c3329d4ace9bd4331e7a888efe975b52fc4" :answer-field/choices ["q-348756/field-1/074131e71753d30c82ed90c556f57c3329d4ace9bd4331e7a888efe975b52fc4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348756" :question/id #uuid "f3844a42-8aa0-5eb9-a1d0-267d67a2e8ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-348756" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14069699/assets/77004c9040818fbc254b9564b9c5821536ef65fcc77f6765b56d2e8524c24ed4.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+1,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nRecall  ${cos}^{2}⁡x+{sin}^{2}⁡x=1,$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2{sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+1 & =4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+2({sin}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3}))+1 \\\\  & =4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(4{cos}^{2}\\,(\\frac{x}{3})+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(2(cos\\,(\\frac{2x}{3})+1)+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3\\pi /2}^{0}(2cos\\,(\\frac{2x}{3})+5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(3sin\\,(\\frac{2x}{3})+5x)\\,|}_{-3\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+5\\cdot 0)-(3sin\\,(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}))+5(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2})) \\\\  & =(0+0)-(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )-\\frac{15\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =(0)-(0-\\frac{15\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348756/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-348844/field-1/04cd542765aba14d4b5f4ba166a29e4f0bd2dccc67d5efe801a574e2c14cf8cb" :answer/id #uuid "70727f01-13ef-5922-aecb-158776ec5560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-348844/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "09c11847-188c-5fd0-96e8-0d9bd3c0d3da" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-348844/field-1/04cd542765aba14d4b5f4ba166a29e4f0bd2dccc67d5efe801a574e2c14cf8cb" :answer-field/choices ["q-348844/field-1/04cd542765aba14d4b5f4ba166a29e4f0bd2dccc67d5efe801a574e2c14cf8cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-348844" :question/id #uuid "889fb234-aee7-55cc-940a-a33b6448e53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-348844" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }6{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above formula as\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{6},$ we have\n\n$$\n1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})=2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6}).\n$$\n\nWe can now integrate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }6{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi }[1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{[x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})]}_{3\\pi }^{6\\pi } \\\\  & =3[6\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6\\pi }{3})-(3\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{3}))] \\\\  & =3[6\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )-(3\\pi -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))] \\\\  & =3(6\\pi -3\\pi ) \\\\  & =9\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-348844/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-348844"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
